{
  "readme": [
    "Parity vectors for the offline till pricer.",
    "",
    "frontend/src/lib/offline/pricing.ts reimplements the part of the Ghana tax",
    "engine that decides WHAT A CUSTOMER OWES. This file is the contract between",
    "that reimplementation and the real engine in backend/src/utils/ghana-tax.ts.",
    "",
    "Two tests read it:",
    "  - backend/src/__tests__/offline-parity.test.ts recomputes every `expected`",
    "    block with computeSaleTax and fails if the server engine has moved.",
    "  - the frontend pricing test runs priceOfflineBasket over the same inputs",
    "    and fails if the offline pricer has moved.",
    "",
    "So a change to either side breaks a build instead of silently changing what a",
    "pharmacy charges while its internet is down.",
    "",
    "`expected` is generated, not hand-written. Regenerate with:",
    "    cd backend && npm run parity:emit",
    "",
    "Items carry no discounts and no product names: the offline pricer refuses a",
    "discounted basket outright (see its docblock), and buildLine's no-discount",
    "path is exactly round2(quantity x unitPrice)."
  ],
  "engine": "backend/src/utils/ghana-tax.ts :: computeSaleTax",
  "generatedBy": "backend/scripts/emit-parity-vectors.ts",
